    "rationale": "Funnel the round into the two families that actually reach the throughput wall. iterative (max 8.84 MSPS) and unrolled_k (max 7.02 MSPS) both produced 0 feasible designs across 40 evals, so they are structurally incapable of the 50 MSPS constraint and should not receive further budget. The feasible front is held solely by pipelined (accuracy extreme, power_index 3.69..4.53, accuracy_bits 12.5..13.6) and pipelined_m (power extreme, 2.78, at data_width=18). Since the selection rule is min power_index and the HV reference power is 40, hypervolume is dominated by how low the power end of the front can be pushed, so the round targets lowering power_index from 2.78 by broadening the barely-mapped pipelined_m region and letting pipelined test cheaper-but-still-accurate points. map_front is deferred to a later round once these ranges are better located."
} 

  ,
  "rationale": "iterative and unrolled_k are dead ends for this spec (0 feasible in 40 evals, best throughputs 8.84 and 7.02 MSPS vs the 50 MSPS requirement). The feasible front lives entirely in pipelined (accuracy tail, power 3.69..4.53) and pipelined_m (power corner 2.78), and pipelined_m was mapped only in a single tiny corner (data_width=18, n_iter=18..19, angle_guard=-1, frac_guard=0..1, m=2; 2 feasible/32 evals). With min power_index as the selection rule and HV reference power 40, the highest-value move is to widen those two families around the low-power corner to find power_index < 2.78 and to fill the accuracy band, before spending a later round on full map_front."
