{
  "decision": "map_front",
  "rationale": "Only pipelined and pipelined_m can meet the 50 MSPS constraint (iterative/unrolled_k top out at 8.84/7.02 MSPS, 0 feasible), so the front is correctly restricted to those two families. But the front is very narrow on both objectives: it spans only data_width 17..20 (accuracy 12.5..15.8 bits) while the registry allows data_width up to 28, and power_index only 1.73..5.85 against the HV reference of 40. The HV (139.3, ref (40,12)) is dominated by the accuracy span — each extra accuracy bit adds ~(40-power)≈35 HV, whereas each unit of power adds only ~(accuracy span)≈3.8 HV — so the unmapped high-accuracy region (data_width 21..28, which the pipelined family should still reach at >50 MSPS given 123 MSPS at W=20) is by far the largest HV gap. A full-range NSGA-II over pipelined/pipelined_m seeded with the current front will extend coverage into that region while preserving the low-power corner (1.73) that the min-power selection rule picks, and leaves round 4 free to refine around that corner."
